# Internationalization (EN + FA)

## Library & Routing

- Use **`next-intl`** with App Router
- Locale prefix: `/en/...` and `/fa/...`
- Default locale: **`en`** (international recruiters); FA equally complete
- `middleware.ts` — locale detection from `Accept-Language` optional; always respect explicit `/fa` or `/en` in URL

```tsx
// Root layout per locale
<html lang={locale} dir={locale === 'fa' ? 'rtl' : 'ltr'}>
```

## Message Files

- `frontend/messages/en.json` and `frontend/messages/fa.json`
- Keys: nested by section — `hero.title`, `projects.viewSite`, `contact.submit`
- Never hardcode user-facing strings in JSX

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<h1>Front-End Developer</h1>

// ✅ GOOD
<h1>{t('hero.title')}</h1>
```

## Language Switcher

- Component: `components/layout/LocaleSwitcher.tsx`
- Preserves current path when switching — `/en/projects` → `/fa/projects`
- Accessible: `aria-label` from i18n; show `EN | FA` or native labels

## RTL (Persian)

- `dir="rtl"` on `<html>` when `locale === 'fa'`
- Use **logical CSS properties:** `margin-inline-start`, `padding-inline`, `text-start`
- Directional icons (chevrons, arrows): flip with `rtl:rotate-180` or logical variants
- Code blocks, URLs, email, phone: `dir="ltr"` + `className="font-mono text-start"`

```css
/* ✅ GOOD */
.section { padding-inline: 1.5rem; margin-inline-start: auto; }

/* ❌ BAD — breaks RTL */
.section { padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-left: auto; }
```

## Typography

- **EN:** professional sans (e.g. Inter via `next/font`)
- **FA:** readable Persian stack (e.g. Vazirmatn or similar via `next/font`)
- Apply locale-specific font in layout based on `locale`
- Line-height ≥ 1.6 for FA body text

## Dates & Numbers

- EN: `Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', …)`
- FA: Jalali optional for blog display (`dayjs` + `jalaliday`); store ISO dates in content frontmatter
- Phone display: LTR always — `+98 903 922 8802` with `dir="ltr"`

## SEO i18n

- Each localized page: correct `lang`, `hreflang` alternates — see `seo.mdc`
- Metadata titles/descriptions from i18n or content frontmatter per locale — not shared English-only metadata

## Content vs UI Strings

| Type | Location |
|------|----------|
| Buttons, labels, nav | `messages/*.json` |
| Blog body | MDX in `content/blog/{locale}/` |
| Projects, experience facts | `content/data/*.ts` with `en` / `fa` fields or separate locale files |

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — structured bilingual project data
export const projects = [
  {
    slug: 'arz-me',
    title: { en: 'Crypto Exchange', fa: 'صرافی ارز' },
    summary: { en: '...', fa: '...' },
    url: 'https://arz.me',
  },
];
```
